      "content": "Booleans"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Booleans are a data type, just like numbers and strings."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "However, unlike numbers and strings, which can represent many values, booleans can only have one of two possible values: true or false."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "javascript",
      "content": "1let result1 = true;\n2let result2 = false;\n3\n4console.log(result1);\n5console.log(result2);"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Output"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "text",
      "content": "true\nfalse"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Here, result1 and result2 are variables storing the true and false boolean value, respectively."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Let's understand booleans in more detail on the next page."
